  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": "Development allocation only, not deployment defaults. ROOT is the current assistant session and is never a worker launch target. Concrete role selections live only here. Provider IDs name the native harness adapter: codex for the Codex CLI (including Ollama-hosted models), claude-code for Claude. Ollama-backed roles explicitly set launch_config.launcher=ollama; the Codex adapter executes `ollama launch codex --model ... --yes --` and omits the duplicate forwarded Codex model flag. Do not implement a separate prefix resolver or change the selected backend. Omitted launcher means direct Codex. Serialize Ollama launches sharing its user profile/catalog directory. Direct Codex selections use the normal service tier. Resolve installed model support, wrapper behavior, authentication, capacity, and provider-home isolation only for the next required role and first affected launch; historical STEP-001 creates no current admission sweep or gate. Fallback for each configured role is ROOT-controlled across separate cleaned-up invocations: every new launch restarts at that role's preferred selection; only an evidenced OAuth error or usage-cap-reached error advances one candidate; all other failures remain on the current candidate under the plan's bounded recovery rules. Fallbacks apply only where explicitly configured for a role. The test_author chain is Claude Opus, then Codex Sol, with its recorded efforts. A prior fallback is never cached as the preferred selection for a later launch. No provider adapter chooses a fallback. APC A and B have identical preferred and fallback bindings; evidence must identify the binding actually used and cannot claim a preferred binding was exercised when a fallback ran. Planning reviewers are outside this execution mapping.",
